# SNES: a game that scribbles its battery RAM continuously is still saved, and
# keeps being saved: the first dump follows the first write, and the core's next
# notice (it re-announces as soon as a dump clears its flag) earns a second dump
# a few seconds later.
expect-screen "TangCore"
press down
press b
expect-screen "game.smc"
press down
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-core snestang
churn on
wram-burst 0x000 512 0xA5
expect-file saves/snes/game.sav size 8192
wait-dump 12s
churn off
